            {
                "entry_id": "e52952f9-acd5-394f-8927-23cd736032d8",
                "word": "Sui",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c13d3df2-a887-3ebc-a1dd-6b8880d8ae07",
                        "entry_id": "e52952f9-acd5-394f-8927-23cd736032d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A county of Suizhou, Hubei, China."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "004440ca-143c-4143-b809-7c97c85c0a86",
                                "sense_id": "c13d3df2-a887-3ebc-a1dd-6b8880d8ae07",
                                "text": "At P’inglin (north-east of the present Sui county, Hupeh), more than one thousand people rose under Ch’en Mu, calling themselves the “P’inglin Army”."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82c8d30d-92ce-48b2-b584-c0190c8a8e59",
                                "sense_id": "c13d3df2-a887-3ebc-a1dd-6b8880d8ae07",
                                "text": "Shen-nung’s geographical origin has been controversial. According to a peasant tradition he was born in a village at the northern border of the county of Sui in Hupei and has been worshipped there (Ching-chou-chi in T’P’YL 189, 6b)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6fbd076-1733-48fd-b375-1d372cfc5550",
                                "sense_id": "c13d3df2-a887-3ebc-a1dd-6b8880d8ae07",
                                "text": "In the past, Mao Pao was ferried across the river [in time of danger] because earlier he had set free a tortoise,⁵ and the marquis of Sui received a pearl because he had saved a snake.⁶\n[...]⁶ Sui was a principality (in Sui County in modern Hupeh Province) in the Warring States period. The marquis of Sui once saved a wounded snake. In return, the snake searched for a large pearl in the river and gave it to the marquis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4417bc8a-4909-41d0-839a-c5c08a27070c",
                                "sense_id": "c13d3df2-a887-3ebc-a1dd-6b8880d8ae07",
                                "text": "By 1985, a volume of the famous scholar Jao Tsung-I/Rao Zongyi (together with Tseng Hsien-tung/Zeng Xiantong) appeared under the title “Studies on the Inscriptions of the Bells and Chimes From the Tomb of Marquis Yi of the Tseng State at Sui-Hsien” (Province of Ho-pei/Hebei, county of Sui)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b27090a2-328b-4f9c-8c56-35e0f5c7904c",
                                "sense_id": "c13d3df2-a887-3ebc-a1dd-6b8880d8ae07",
                                "text": "Mr Zeng returned to Sui county, about 200km north of Wuhan, on January 21 to celebrate the Chinese new year with his parents.[...]“If the disease drags on for two months, the start-up I work for will go under and I’ll lose my job,” he said. “There is nothing I can do about this except hope the epidemic will end soon. I am ready to spend a few months in Sui County.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
